Q: How to fully reset mat-input with mat-autocomplete A: <p>Found a better alternative without needing the set timeout.</p>
<p>Listen to the <a href="https://angular.dev/guide/templates/event-listeners#listening-to-native-events" rel="nofollow noreferrer">event</a> and call the control .updateValueAndValidity() method. This will trigger change detection on the control, open the associated autocomplete panel and clears the active option.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;mat-form-field&gt;
      &lt;mat-label&gt;example&lt;/mat-label&gt;
      &lt;input matInput type=&quot;text&quot; 
          [matAutocomplete]=&quot;autocomplete&quot;
          formControlName=&quot;example&quot;
          (focus)=&quot;form.controls.example.updateValueAndValidity()&quot;&gt;
      &lt;mat-autocomplete #autocomplete=&quot;matAutocomplete&quot;
          (optionSelected)=&quot;selectionMade($event)&quot; &gt;
          @for (pl of (filteredPlans$ | async) ?? []; track pl;) {
          &lt;mat-option [value]=&quot;pl&quot;&gt;{{ pl.label}}&lt;/mat-option&gt;
          }
     &lt;/mat-autocomplete&gt;
&lt;/mat-form-field&gt;
</code></pre>
